{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vlpi5qonovx2zizws4m3etr2s3fluarkowjeakp2jpt7nbbel5jq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. Here's the summary:\n\n## What was built\n\nThe crate was binary-only with no library, no exports, and **no features**, so I added a `[lib] crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` target (`src/lib.rs` + `src/ffi.rs`) that exports the C ABI, moved the driver logic into `src/driver.rs` so the binary and the `.so` run *identical* code, and built the C side as a `.so` from the unmodified `c_src/src/*.c`.\n\n**Artifacts** (crate root): `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `check_features.sh`.\n\n## Results per phase\n\n- **A — surface map.** 16 C symbols (`tokenizer.c` + `analyzer.c` + `main.c`, incl. `main`); struct layouts verified against a C `offsetof` probe (`token_t` = 280 B, memory-class return). 45 `ERRORS.md` rows + 9 generic-FFI rows; 55 `CONFIGS.md` rows.\n- **B — valid paths.** 103 differential tests, every call through `dlsym` on both `.so`s (never a direct Rust call), driven from the lowest level up (`load_text`/`next_token`/`peek_token`/`reset`/`get_stats`, then through `get_tokenizer_ops`' function pointers, then the analyzer, then `main.c`'s functions, then the full REPL), with seeded random corpora (all 255 single bytes, byte pairs, ~1000 random texts, 400-step peek/next scripts, 60 random menu scripts).\n- **C — error paths.** Every `ERRORS.md` row asserts the *same* sentinel and the *same* stderr text (fd 1 and 2 captured per library), incl. NULL pointers everywhere, 8191/8192/8193 boundaries, interior NULs, non-UTF-8 paths, and out-of-enum token types across the FFI. Only E33 (`malloc` failure) is untested — unprovokable without a fault injector.\n- **D — parity & combos.** `nm -D` diff is **empty** (0/16 missing, 1 extra test-only symbol) in debug *and* release. `check_features.sh` runs `check --all-targets` + `build` + `test` for both combinations (`default`, `--no-default-features`) × both profiles: **412 test-case executions, 0 failures.**\n\n## Real divergences found and fixed (Rust only; C untouched)\n\n1. **NULL `tokenizer_ops_t` dispatch** — C dies from `SIGSEGV` with its buffered stdout discarded; Rust printed a panic + backtrace and died from `SIGABRT`. Now faults identically (signal + output asserted).\n2. **`SIGPIPE`** — `driver | head -c 64`: C died with signal 13, Rust exited 0 (the Rust runtime ignores `SIGPIPE`). `main` now restores the default disposition.\n3. **Prompt flush on an interactive terminal** — glibc flushes line-buffered stdout before reading line-buffered stdin, so `\"Choice: Enter filename: \"` precedes a `read_file` stderr message; Rust emitted it after. `cio` now mirrors `_IO_new_file_underflow`, and takes its buffer size from `st_blksize` like `_IO_file_doallocate`.\n\nTwo *harness* bugs that were hiding failures were also fixed: a stale `cdylib` was being compared (`cargo test --test X` doesn't rebuild a lib nothing links), and libtest's own progress lines leaked into fd-1 captures. Each fix was validated by mutation testing (e.g. a one-character change to a printf string or the column arithmetic fails 40+ tests)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":146,"cache_read_input_tokens":391239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":146,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5a5c366-7b13-48c9-a820-e7aa27b1e5c6","uuid":"98561506-ebe1-4d73-898a-ce5803a71fec","timestamp":"2026-08-20T00:08:53.311Z"}
